'''Great Migration''', '''Great Migrations''', or '''The Great Migration''' may refer to:
{{tocright}}
==Historical events==
* Great Migration of [[Catharist migration to Abayla|Cathars from the Mesogean to Abyala]] (1568–1760)
* Great Migration of Black Kaftians, resulting from the 18xx [[Partition of Lacashe]] and independence of [[Libertalia]]
* Baliscan "Great Migrations":
** The original [[Great Migration (Balisca)]] from overseas to the [[Northern Triangle]] (c. 1860–1920), sometimes called the Great Baliscan Migration
** The [[Second Great Migration (Balisca)]] from countries affected by the [[Great Adonian War]], drawn by lax regulations under the policy of {{W|free migration}} and the [[Baliscan economic miracle|post-war economic boom]] (1947–1970)
** The [[New Great Migration]], post-COVID migration surge into Balisca, amidst the [[Baliscan housing shortage]] (2022–present)

